    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field derived from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else UNKNOWN).\n\nThe response DTO is generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct, so the change touched three places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` gets a `locality` field on generation).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../util/Locality.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper holding the fixed `CITY_REGION` table with `Locality.of(city)` returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping(target = \"locality\", expression = \"java(...Locality.of(owner.getCity()))\")` alongside the other derived-field mappings, so both the create (`POST`) and read (`GET`) responses carry it.\n\nResults:\n- The two new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 Sydney/NSW, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 UNKNOWN) pass.\n- Full suite: **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nThis slots into the existing OfficeFloor pipeline without new functions \u2014 the derivation lives in the mapper that both `RespondWithOwner` and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` already use.",
